      "side": 1,
      "message": "`exp_rate` is value we expect that driver will set for given `rate` and rounding `rnd`. The switch case convert `exp_rate` to value which we expect that was written by driver to device register. `BMA2x2_BW_*` defines are in range `[0x8-0xf]`. Real hardware will treat values smaller than 0x8 as 0x8 and greater than 0xf as 0xf, but it is not recommended to use that behaviour (for compatibility with other BMA* devices).\n\nUsing different values for `exp_rate` doesn\u0027t make sense, because driver should never set rate not supported by the BMA255 accelerometer.\n\nIf `exp_rate` is not one of values from switch case, then it is error in unit test, not in driver. I may add here assert with appropriate message.",
